.TH CLOCK 1 "Peios" "timed 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clock \- inspect and control the Peios time client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clock
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clock
queries the machine-wide
.BR timed (8)
service over its local control socket.  With no command it displays the
current synchronisation status.
.PP
Time-source policy is registry configuration under
.BR Machine\\System\\Time .
Change it with
.BR reg (1),
then ask the daemon to reload it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show synchronisation state, selected peer, offset, frequency, jitter,
accuracy, update count, and the build-time clock floor.
.TP
.B sources
List configured sources, their authentication and reachability, and their
part in source selection.
.TP
.B reload
Re-read
.B Machine\\System\\Time
and poll immediately.  This operation requires control access to timed's
control object.
.TP
.BR help , " -h" , " --help"
Show command help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The request completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The daemon was unavailable or refused the request.
.TP
.B 2
The requested information was absent, for example when no sources are
configured.
.TP
.B 64
The command line was not understood.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /run/timed/time.sock
Local timed control socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timed (8),
.BR reg (1)
